# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OwnRAG — environment files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# OwnRAG has no single root .env. Each component reads its own file, and each
# one ships an example next to it. Copy the example you need, then edit the copy.
#
#   engine/.env.example     the local engine: host/port, the owner account,
#                           CORS origins, chunking, optional model endpoints.
#                           Copy to engine/.env
#
#   docker/.env             the preserved backend's compose stack (datastores,
#                           image tags, service passwords). Copy from
#                           docker/.env.single-bucket-example or edit in place.
#
#   web/                    needs no environment file for local development:
#                           the dev server proxies /api and /v1 to
#                           http://127.0.0.1:9380 (see web/vite.config.ts).
#
# Never commit a real .env. The root .gitignore ignores `.env` and `.env.*.local`, the
# per-component ignore files cover the rest, and the only env files in the repository are
# examples and templates (docker/.env is the upstream compose template, with placeholder
# passwords that must be changed before any non-local deployment).
#
# The secrets an own deployment ends up holding are:
#   - provider API keys for chat/embedding/rerank models: stored in the engine
#     database (engine/data/ownrag.db) when added through the console, or in
#     engine/.env as deployment defaults
#   - datastore passwords for the preserved backend: docker/.env
#   - the owner account password for a network-exposed engine:
#     OWNRAG_OWNER_PASSWORD in engine/.env (the engine refuses to bind a
#     non-loopback address without it)
